// AE 1.7.104 store-site tables. Every entry's bytes are verified before anything is patched.
//
// The hidden-store table is a program-wide scan of the 1.7.104 executable (a linear disassembly of .text, restarted at every
// .pdata function start) for writes to `[reg + 0xf4]`:
//  - every `or` that may set bit 0;
//  - every `and` that may clear it;
//  - every `mov` of any width (the stub compares bit 0 itself).
// The same scan of 1.6.1170 finds every entry of that table, and of 1.5.97 every entry of its table; as there, `add`/`inc`
// counters are left out, and so are RSP-based sites, because the stub's call moves RSP.
// Some sites are not an NiAVObject's (stack slots, other classes); their events carry keys no scene object has.
// Main::Draw's and TESWaterReflections::Update's stores hide a node and show it again within one frame, around views (the
// first-person skeleton; the water shapes and the player's 3D). They are kept, one event per store, and never merged or dropped:
// see the README's "Hides within a frame".
// The switch-index, fade-reset and show tables are 1.6.1170's, each site found again in its function (by Address Library id; the
// object LOD segment updates were renumbered), the same occurrence of its bytes there. Neither store has a new site: 1.7.104's
// only new integer store to +0x12C is a field-by-field copy, and the fade reset's store-then-bit-14 pattern has the same twelve
// sites as on 1.6.1170 (the eleven below, and the fade update's own, which the fade calls family hooks).
// Comments name the function (1.6.1170's name where it has one, else its 1.7.104 address) and the instruction (dword unless
// stated).
//
// Table order is the event's site index; keep it stable within a release.
#include "tables/StoreSites.h"

